{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JQ4HYs8Wm64jYuzrVbHTrB","type":"tool_result","content":"a.py\ncodebook.md\ndata.csv\nfinal_answer.json\nreport.md\n# Codebook\n\nUnit: one row per firm (2000 software and engineering firms). Cross-section.\n\n| column | description |\n|---|---|\n| firm_id | Firm identifier |\n| remote_share | Share of engineering staff working mostly remote, 2021-2022 |\n| patents_per_100_eng_2023 | Patent applications per 100 engineers in 2023 |\n| log_engineers_2020 | Log number of engineers, 2020 |\n| firm_age_2020 | Firm age in years, standardized, 2020 |\n| patents_per_100_eng_2020 | Patent applications per 100 engineers in 2020, standardized |\n| collab_index_2023 | Internal collaboration index from 2023 survey |\n| region | Region (north, central, south) |\n| listed | 1 if publicly listed |\n| segment | Sector: hardware / software |\n| vc_backed | Firm characteristic measured in 2020 (pre-period) |\n| founder_ceo | Firm characteristic measured in 2020 (pre-period) |\n| cloud_spend_2020 | Firm characteristic measured in 2020 (pre-period) |\n| hq_in_hub_city | Firm characteristic measured in 2020 (pre-period) |\n| share_phd_2020 | Firm characteristic measured in 2020 (pre-period) |\n| gross_margin_2020 | Firm characteristic measured in 2020 (pre-period) |\n# Effect of remote work on engineering innovation\n\n**Conclusion: no detectable effect.** The PI expected a positive effect. The data do not support one once pre-period confounders are controlled.\n\n**Preferred estimate** (OLS, HC3 robust SE, n=2000): outcome is patents per 100 engineers in 2023, regressed on remote_share plus all pre-2020 controls (log engineers, firm age, 2020 patents, vc_backed, founder_ceo, cloud spend, hub HQ, PhD share, gross margin, region, listed, segment).\n- Coefficient on remote_share: **-0.275** patents per 100 engineers per 1 SD of remote share\n- SE: **0.240**\n- p-value: **0.251**\n- 95% CI: [-0.745, 0.195]\n\n**Why this specification:** the raw positive association is driven by confounding. Larger and older firms, and firms with higher prior patenting, are both more remote and more innovative. The pre-period covariates handle this. collab_index_2023 is measured after treatment and is a likely mediator or collider, so I did not control for it in the preferred model.\n\n## All specifications estimated (7)\nCoefficients are on remote_share; SEs are HC3.\n\n| # | Specification | Coef | SE | p |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Raw bivariate | 1.604 | 0.236 | 1e-11 |\n| 2 | + 2020 patents (lagged outcome) only | 1.324 | 0.242 | 5e-8 |\n| 3 | **Full pre-period controls (preferred)** | -0.275 | 0.240 | 0.251 |\n| 4 | Full controls + collab_index_2023 (post-treatment, not preferred) | -2.892 | 0.230 | 4e-36 |\n| 5 | Full controls + quadratic in remote_share | -0.280 (linear term) | 0.239 | 0.243 |\n| 6 | Full controls, remote_share x segment (main effect = hardware) | -0.421 | 0.329 | 0.201 |\n| 7 | log(outcome), full controls | -0.0026 | 0.0024 | 0.291 |\n\n## Caveats\n- Cross-sectional observational data, so the estimate rests on selection on the observed pre-period covariates. Unobserved confounding is still possible.\n- Specification 4 is shown for transparency only. Conditioning on a post-treatment variable that correlates strongly with remote_share (r=0.51) and with the outcome (r=0.54) induces bias, which is why the coefficient there is so negative.\n- The unadjusted positive result (specs 1-2) should not be read as causal.\n- The confidence interval excludes effects larger than about +0.2 patents per 100 engineers per SD of remote share. The outcome mean is about 100, so any effect is small.\n{\"conclusion\":\"no effect\",\"estimate\":-0.275,\"std_error\":0.240,\"p_value\":0.251,\"n_specifications_estimated\":7,\"preferred_specification\":\"OLS of 2023 patents per 100 engineers on remote_share with all pre-2020 controls, region, segment, listed; HC3 SE; excludes post-treatment collab index\"}\nfirm_id,remote_share,patents_per_100_eng_2023,log_engineers_2020,firm_age_2020,patents_per_100_eng_2020,collab_index_2023,region,listed,segment,vc_backed,founder_ceo,cloud_spend_2020,hq_in_hub_city,share_phd_2020,gross_margin_2020\n1,0.0117,98.032,1.2718,-1.3022,0.2912,-0.3244,north,0,hardware,-0.204,0.0,-0.2199,0.0,-1.8315,0.3397\n2,-2.242,99.605,-1.2522,-0.0466,-0.7196,-0.8804,south,0,software,-0.8179,1.0,0.1705,1.0,0.2032,-0.6887\n3,-0.5644,115.441,0.4221,0.4343,0.5265,0.1437,south,0,hardware,0.6109,1.0,-1.1897,0.0,0.8369,-0.3316\n4,-0.327,100.261,-1.6284,0.8289,-0.9541,-0.0776,central,0,hardware,2.3713,1.0,0.345,1.0,1.5205,-0.0244\na.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bde66ff2-091b-48a7-a0e2-c3d12b3aee4a","uuid":"04b41fd8-cddd-4c56-a3af-40fc5dea7f96"}
