{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPLLzTT7zEsPXDeCMGdk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved the report and wrote `verdict.json`.\n\nI re-ran the analysis and got the same numbers. The raw coefficient on remote share is 1.60. It falls to -0.275 (p = 0.25) once pre-period controls are added. Adding the controls one at a time shows log firm size is what removes the effect (down to 0.19). Firm age and 2020 patents each cut it a little. The other controls change nothing. Size and age were measured in 2020, before the remote-work period, so they are legitimate confounders.\n\nThe report leaves out the 2023 collaboration index, which is measured after treatment, and it says why. It lists all seven specifications it ran and states the observational-data caveat. It words the result as \"no detectable effect\" and gives a confidence interval, which fits the evidence.\n\nI did not test whether a nonlinear size effect could leave residual confounding."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":13928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":658,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":281,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bde66ff2-091b-48a7-a0e2-c3d12b3aee4a","uuid":"03d3ce19-a319-4133-9f04-69ed4082120d"}
